#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:46
msgid ""
"`pinkie` exports bare [ES2015 "
"Promise](https://people.mozilla.org/~jorendorff/es6-draft.html#sec-"
"promise-objects) implementation and polyfills [Node.js rejection "
"events](https://nodejs.org/api/process.html#process_event_unhandledrejection)."
" In case you forgot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:48
msgid "new Promise(executor)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:50
msgid "Returns new instance of `Promise`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:52
msgid "executor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:54
msgid "*Required*   Type: `function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:57
msgid ""
"Function with two arguments `resolve` and `reject`. The first argument "
"fulfills the promise, the second argument rejects it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:59
msgid "pinkie.all(promises)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:61
msgid ""
"Returns a promise that resolves when all of the promises in the "
"`promises` Array argument have resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:63
msgid "pinkie.race(promises)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:65
msgid ""
"Returns a promise that resolves or rejects as soon as one of the promises"
" in the `promises` Array resolves or rejects, with the value or reason "
"from that promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:67
msgid "pinkie.reject(reason)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:69
msgid "Returns a Promise object that is rejected with the given `reason`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:71
msgid "pinkie.resolve(value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pinkie_readme.md:73
msgid ""
"Returns a Promise object that is resolved with the given `value`. If the "
"`value` is a thenable (i.e. has a then method), the returned promise will"
" \"follow\" that thenable, adopting its eventual state; otherwise the "
"returned promise will be fulfilled with the `value`."
msgstr ""

